  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Design Concepts**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to visualize this React app. I\'m focusing on the structural elements first: the top banner with that crucial timer and subject tabs, and the question viewport. KaTeX is the key for rendering the math questions. I\'m also thinking about user-friendliness and responsiveness.\n\n\n**Adding Question Interaction**\n\nI\'ve been concentrating on the user\'s interaction with the questions. I\'m incorporating those action buttons: Save & Next, Mark for Review & Next, and Clear Response. The question palette is also taking shape. I\'m focusing on those 75 buttons and the color states. Per-question timing telemetry will also be tracked in local state.\n\n\n**Incorporating Math Rendering**\n\nI\'m now integrating KaTeX. It needs to be a dependency, so I\'ll install it using install_applet_package. I\'ll need to check if I also require `@types/katex`. Additionally, I will install katex and import the CSS.\n\nI\'m examining the structure of the NTA JEE Main CBT UI. I\'ve noted a distinctive header with the \"JEE (Main)\" title, candidate details, a language selector, and subject tabs. The crucial countdown timer is also prominent. Also important: The section structure must support distinct question type sections, for example, multiple-choice questions (MCQs), and numerical types.\n\n\n**Defining Question Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now drilling down into individual question details. I\'m focusing on the No. indicator, the marks breakdown, and section types. I\'ll need to render LaTeX equations across the board, covering a wide range of subjects. I\'m thinking about radio buttons for MCQs, and numeric input for those questions. The action buttons are also locked in: \"Save & Next\", \"Mark for Review & Next\", and \"Clear Response\", and I\'ll include back/next navigation. Finally, the question palette will use precise NTA legend states.\n\n\n"
