  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Interface Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the NTA JEE Main interface. Currently, I\'m breaking down the top banner. I\'m focusing on the header bar, and specifically, the exam name display and candidate name formatting. Details such as the title \"JEE(Main) - 2025\" are being noted.\n\n\n**Examining the Header Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the right side of the header. I\'ve noted the candidate photo placeholder, the candidate info format (name, roll, system), and the countdown timer display. Specifically, I\'m considering the format: \"Time Left : 179:45\" (from 180 minutes), and how it compares to standard NTA CBT timer designs, along with the availability of pause/resume functionality. Finally, I\'m noting the subject switch tabs (Physics, Chemistry, Math), and their usual placement and potential subsection structure (\"Section A\", \"Section B\").\n\n\n**Detailing the Question Display**\n\nI\'m now deep into the question viewport. The header bar\'s elements are under scrutiny: question number, language dropdown (English/Hindi), marking scheme, and time spent indicator are noted. Font size adjuster buttons (A-, A, A+) are confirmed as well. The primary focus is now on how LaTeX is rendered via KaTeX for complex equations across physics and chemistry, from projectile motion to reaction kinetics.\n\n\n**Assessing Formula Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on equation rendering. My focus is primarily on how complex LaTeX is handled, covering a diverse set of examples. These include physics equations, thermodynamics, and organic chemistry reactions and formulas, along with mathematical expressions. I\'m verifying the display of equations within multiple-choice options.\n\n**Evaluating Interaction Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m analyzing the question interaction methods, specifically the action buttons. The standard NTA button set is present: Save & Next, Clear Response, and Save & Mark for Review. I\'m looking for a clear definition of how each button changes question status, and what happens on the backend based on those selections.\n\n\n**Defining Button Behaviors**\n\nI am now focusing on the action buttons, and have a good grasp on how the \"Save & Mark for Review\" button operates; saving the answer, marking it as \"Answered & Marked for Review\", and advancing to the next. The system behaves similarly to \"Mark for Review & Next,\" but *without* an answer selected, the mark is \"Marked for Review.\" Standard \"Back/Previous\" and \"Next\" buttons are also present for navigation.\n\n**Mapping Question States**\n\nI am now analyzing the question palette on the right side. The question layout across Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics is now very clear, from Q1-25, 26-50, and 51-75. I\'ve noted the 5 NTA color states for the questions. Specifically, I\'m documenting the appearance of \"Not Visited,\" \"Not Answered,\" and \"Answered\" and how they are indicated on the interface.\n\n\n**Documenting Interface States**\n\nI\'m now detailing the question palette indicators. I\'ve documented the purple color (`#7c3aed` and `#6b21a8`) for \"Answered & Marked for Review\", with its green checkmark. I\'ve also noted the dynamic legend box counts and its states. I\'m focusing now on how question state changes upon visiting, and also documenting the collapse/expand palette button. I\'m also planning per-question timing telemetry in local state.\n\n\n**Implementing Test Data and Metrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating the mock test features. The real-time question header showing elapsed time is functional. The detailed telemetry, including time spent per question and subject-wise stats, will be accessible via an \"Exam Summary\" or \"Submit Test\" modal. I\'m focusing on the implementation details and how to make the reset button function.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1052034"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"export type Subject = \'Physics\' | \'Chemistry\' | \'Mathematics\';\\n\\nexport type QuestionType = \'MCQ\' | \'NUMERICAL\';\\n\\nexport type QuestionStatus = \\n  | \'NOT_VISITED\'\\n  | \'NOT_ANSWERED\'\\n  | \'ANSWERED\'\\n  | \'MARKED_FOR_REVIEW\'\\n  | \'ANSWERED_AND_MARKED\';\\n\\nexport interface Option {\\n  id: string; // \'1\' | \'2\' | \'3\' | \'4\'\\n  label: string; // text or LaTeX\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Question {\\n  id: number; // 1 to 75\\n  subject: Subject;\\n  section: \'Section A\' | \'Section B\'; // Section A: MCQ (1-20), Section B: Numerical (21-25)\\n  type: QuestionType;\\n  questionText: string;\\n  options?: Option[]; // for MCQ\\n  correctAnswer: string; // \'1\',\'2\',\'3\',\'4\' or numerical value e.g. \'25\'\\n  explanation?: string;\\n  marks: {\\n    correct: number;\\n    incorrect: number;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface QuestionTelemetry {\\n  timeSpentSeconds: number; // total time spent on this question\\n  visitCount: number;\\n  lastVisitedTimestamp?: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ExamState {\\n  currentQuestionId: number;\\n  currentSubject: Subject;\\n  answers: Record<number, string>; // questionId -> selectedOptionId or numerical answer\\n  statuses: Record<number, QuestionStatus>; // questionId -> status\\n  telemetry: Record<number, QuestionTelemetry>; // questionId -> telemetry\\n  remainingTimeSeconds: number; // 180 min * 60 = 10800\\n  isTimerRunning: boolean;\\n  isExamSubmitted: boolean;\\n  language: \'English\' | \'Hindi\';\\n  fontSize: \'small\' | \'medium\' | \'large\';\\n}\\n\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating types file\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create types.ts\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "create_file"
    }
