        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A particle of mass $m$ is projected with velocity $v_0$ at an angle $\\\\theta = 45^\\\\circ$ with the horizontal from the ground. The magnitude of angular momentum of the projectile about the point of projection when the particle is at its maximum height is:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$\\\\frac{m v_0^3}{4\\\\sqrt{2} g}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$\\\\frac{m v_0^3}{2\\\\sqrt{2} g}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$\\\\frac{m v_0^3}{\\\\sqrt{2} g}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$\\\\frac{m v_0^2}{4 g}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'At maximum height, $H = \\\\frac{v_0^2 \\\\sin^2(45^\\\\circ)}{2g} = \\\\frac{v_0^2}{4g}$. The velocity is horizontal: $v_x = v_0 \\\\cos(45^\\\\circ) = \\\\frac{v_0}{\\\\sqrt{2}}$. Angular momentum $L = m v_x H = m \\\\left(\\\\frac{v_0}{\\\\sqrt{2}}\\\\right) \\\\left(\\\\frac{v_0^2}{4g}\\\\right) = \\\\frac{m v_0^3}{4\\\\sqrt{2}g}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
