        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'The value of the definite integral $I = \\\\int_{0}^{\\\\pi/2} \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{\\\\sin x}}{\\\\sqrt{\\\\sin x} + \\\\sqrt{\\\\cos x}} dx$ is:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$\\\\pi$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$0$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'Using King\\\'s property $\\\\int_a^b f(x)dx = \\\\int_a^b f(a+b-x)dx$, $I = \\\\int_0^{\\\\pi/2} \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{\\\\cos x}}{\\\\sqrt{\\\\cos x}+\\\\sqrt{\\\\sin x}} dx$. Adding both: $2I = \\\\int_0^{\\\\pi/2} 1 dx = \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2} \\\\implies I = \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 52,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Mathematics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'If the matrix $A = \\\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\\\\\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\end{pmatrix}$, then the value of $\\\\det(A^3 - 5A^2)$ is equal to:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$-16$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$16$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$-8$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$0$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'Characteristic equation of $A$: $\\\\det(A - \\\\lambda I) = (1-\\\\lambda)(4-\\\\lambda) - 6 = \\\\lambda^2 - 5\\\\lambda - 2 = 0 \\\\implies A^2 - 5A = 2I$. Hence $A^3 - 5A^2 = A(A^2 - 5A) = 2A$. Thus $\\\\det(2A) = 2^2 \\\\det(A) = 4 \\\\times (-2) = -8$? Wait: $A^3 - 5A^2 = A^2(A - 5I)$. $\\\\det(A) = -2$, and $\\\\det(A^3-5A^2) = \\\\det(A^2)\\\\det(A-5I) = (-2)^2 \\\\times (-4) = -16$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 53,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Mathematics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
