        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'The shortest distance between the skew lines $\\\\vec{r} = \\\\hat{i} + \\\\lambda(2\\\\hat{i} - \\\\hat{j} + \\\\hat{k})$ and $\\\\vec{r} = 2\\\\hat{i} - \\\\hat{k} + \\\\mu(3\\\\hat{i} - 5\\\\hat{j} + 2\\\\hat{k})$ is determined by the formula $d = \\\\frac{|(\\\\vec{a}_2 - \\\\vec{a}_1) \\\\cdot (\\\\vec{b}_1 \\\\times \\\\vec{b}_2)|}{|\\\\vec{b}_1 \\\\times \\\\vec{b}_2|}$. The cross product $\\\\vec{b}_1 \\\\times \\\\vec{b}_2$ is:\',"
