  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "This session has focused on building a single-page React application that mimics the official NTA JEE Main computer-based testing (CBT) interface. The implementation is modular, with all core UI components created and ready for orchestration.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Status: IMPLEMENTATION**\n- **Request:** \"Build a single-page React app mimicking the official NTA JEE Main computer-based testing interface.\"\n  - (1) Top banner with candidate timer (countdown from 180 min), subject switch tabs (Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics).\n  - (2) Question viewport rendering LaTeX via KaTeX.\n  - (3) Action buttons: \'Save & Next\', \'Mark for Review & Next\', \'Clear Response\'.\n  - (4) Right sidebar Question Palette (75 buttons) with the 5 official NTA color states: Not Visited, Not Answered (Red), Answered (Green), Marked for Review (Purple), Answered & Marked (Purple with green check).\n  - (5) Include per-question timing telemetry in local state.\n- **Status:** All UI components (`Header`, `QuestionViewport`, `ActionFooter`, `QuestionPalette`, `ExamSummaryModal`, `KaTeXRenderer`) have been implemented. The final step is to integrate these into `App.tsx` with the necessary state management logic.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **None stated.** The user provided the initial prompt and file tree, but no specific constraints or preferences beyond the functional requirements.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Setup:**\n  - Installed `katex` and `@types/katex`.\n  - Updated `metadata.json` and `index.html` (added KaTeX CSS, meta tags, and body classes).\n- **Architecture & Components:**\n  - Defined core types in `/src/types.ts` (`ExamState`, `Question`, `QuestionStatus`, etc.).\n  - Created a comprehensive question bank in `/src/data/questions.ts` (75 questions: 25 Physics, 25 Chemistry, 25 Mathematics).\n  - Implemented `KaTeXRenderer` for LaTeX support.\n  - Implemented `NTAStateBadge` for the palette UI.\n  - Implemented `Header` (timer, subject tabs, language toggle).\n  - Implemented `QuestionViewport` (question display, MCQ/Numerical inputs, font scaling).\n  - Implemented `ActionFooter` (navigation, action buttons).\n  - Implemented `QuestionPalette` (sidebar with status legend and 75-question grid).\n  - Implemented `ExamSummaryModal` (submission summary, telemetry, solutions).\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:** The app is designed as a single-page React application. State management (timer, answers, statuses, telemetry) is intended to be centralized in `App.tsx`.\n- **Telemetry:** The `ExamState` type tracks `telemetry` (time spent, visit count) per question ID.\n- **Constraints:** The app handles 75 questions, categorized by subject and section (A/B).\n- **Dependencies:** Uses `lucide-react` for icons, `katex` for math rendering, and `tailwindcss` for styling.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited/Created Files:**\n  - `/metadata.json`: Updated metadata.\n  - `/index.html`: Added KaTeX CSS and body classes.\n  - `/src/types.ts`: Created core types.\n  - `/src/components/KaTeXRenderer.tsx`: Created LaTeX renderer.\n  - `/src/data/questions.ts`: Created question bank.\n  - `/src/components/NTAStateBadge.tsx`: Created status badge component.\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Created header component.\n  - `/src/components/QuestionViewport.tsx`: Created viewport component.\n  - `/src/components/ActionFooter.tsx`: Created footer component.\n  - `/src/components/QuestionPalette.tsx`: Created palette component.\n  - `/src/components/ExamSummaryModal.tsx`: Created summary modal component.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/package.json`: Verified dependencies.\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Initial entry point (currently empty).\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Next Steps:**\n  - Implement the main logic in `/src/App.tsx`.\n  - Initialize `ExamState` (timer, questions, statuses).\n  - Implement the timer logic (countdown from 180 min).\n  - Connect all components (`Header`, `QuestionViewport`, `ActionFooter`, `QuestionPalette`, `ExamSummaryModal`) to the central state.\n  - Implement navigation and status update logic (e.g., \'Save & Next\' updates the status to \'ANSWERED\', increments the timer, etc.).\n- **Relevant Files:**\n  - `/src/App.tsx` (Needs implementation).\n  - `/src/types.ts` (Reference for state structure).\n  - `/src/data/questions.ts` (Reference for question data)."
    included_step_index_end: 28
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/dacfb59c-b93b-475c-987d-b7e1d4cb3135/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "User prompt: Build a single-page React app mimicking the official NTA JEE Main computer-based testing interface. Include: (1) Top banner with candidate timer (countdown from 180 min), subject switch tabs (Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics). (2) Question viewport rendering LaTeX via KaTeX. (3) Action buttons: \'Save & Next\', \'Mark for Review & Next\', \'Clear Response\'. (4) Right sidebar Question Palette (75 buttons) with the 5 official NTA color states: Not Visited, Not Answered (Red), Answered (Green), Marked for Review (Purple), Answered & Marked (Purple with green check). Include per-question timing telemetry in local state.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "Build a single-page React app mimicking the official NTA JEE Main computer-based testing interface. Include: (1) Top banner with candidate timer (countdown from 180 min), subject switch tabs (Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics). (2) Question viewport rendering LaTeX via KaTeX. (3) Action buttons: \'Save & Next\', \'Mark for Review & Next\', \'Clear Response\'. (4) Right sidebar Question Palette (75 buttons) with the 5 official NTA color states: Not Visited, Not Answered (Red), Answered (Green), Marked for Review (Purple), Answered & Marked (Purple with green check). Include per-question timing telemetry in local state."
