  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the single-page application mimicking the official **NTA JEE Main Computer-Based Testing (CBT)** interface:\n\n- **Top Banner & Candidate Countdown**:\n  - Implemented an authentic NTA examination header displaying candidate credentials, roll number, and live digital countdown timer configured from 180 minutes (with pause/resume controls for mock sessions).\n  - Integrated subject switch tabs for **Physics** (Q1\342\200\22325), **Chemistry** (Q26\342\200\22350), and **Mathematics** (Q51\342\200\22375) with real-time answered/total ratio badges.\n  - Added quick toggles for bilingual view (English/Hindi), official CBT instructions modal, and full question paper overview.\n\n- **Question Viewport with KaTeX LaTeX Engine**:\n  - Rendered authentic JEE Main question papers with mathematical and chemical notations using KaTeX for fractions, integrals, matrices, limits, vectors, and chemical structures.\n  - Included marking scheme badges (`+4.00`, `-1.00`), font size adjusters (`A-`, `A`, `A+`), and interactive single-choice radio options.\n  - Provided an on-screen virtual numeric keypad for Section B numerical questions.\n\n- **CBT Action Control Bar**:\n  - **Save & Next**: Commits the candidate\'s response, marks the status as **Answered** (Green), and advances to the next question.\n  - **Mark for Review & Next**: Marks the question as **Answered & Marked** (Purple with green checkmark) if an option is selected, or **Marked for Review** (Purple circle) if unselected, advancing forward.\n  - **Clear Response**: Clears selected options and resets the status back to **Not Answered** (Red).\n  - **Back / Next & Submit**: Standard NTA navigation controls.\n\n- **Question Palette (75 Questions) & 5 Official NTA States**:\n  - Designed the right sidebar housing all 75 question buttons with official shapes and colors:\n    1. **Not Visited**: Neutral white/slate with border\n    2. **Not Answered**: Official NTA Red\n    3. **Answered**: Official NTA Green\n    4. **Marked for Review**: Official NTA Purple circle\n    5. **Answered & Marked for Review**: Purple circle with an overlaid bright green checkmark badge *(considered for evaluation)*\n  - Live summary counter box reflecting instantaneous counts across all 5 states.\n  - Collapsible sidebar toggle to expand question viewport to full-width when needed.\n\n- **Per-Question Timing Telemetry in Local State**:\n  - Integrated active per-question timers tracking exact seconds and visit counts for each of the 75 questions in local state and persistent browser storage.\n  - Displayed a live timer on the active question viewport (`Time: MM:SS`).\n  - Added an **Exam Summary & Telemetry Analytics Modal** providing subject-wise breakdown tables, per-question duration logs, average time per question, and post-submission scoring with detailed solutions."
    modified_response: "I have completed the single-page application mimicking the official **NTA JEE Main Computer-Based Testing (CBT)** interface:\n\n- **Top Banner & Candidate Countdown**:\n  - Implemented an authentic NTA examination header displaying candidate credentials, roll number, and live digital countdown timer configured from 180 minutes (with pause/resume controls for mock sessions).\n  - Integrated subject switch tabs for **Physics** (Q1\342\200\22325), **Chemistry** (Q26\342\200\22350), and **Mathematics** (Q51\342\200\22375) with real-time answered/total ratio badges.\n  - Added quick toggles for bilingual view (English/Hindi), official CBT instructions modal, and full question paper overview.\n\n- **Question Viewport with KaTeX LaTeX Engine**:\n  - Rendered authentic JEE Main question papers with mathematical and chemical notations using KaTeX for fractions, integrals, matrices, limits, vectors, and chemical structures.\n  - Included marking scheme badges (`+4.00`, `-1.00`), font size adjusters (`A-`, `A`, `A+`), and interactive single-choice radio options.\n  - Provided an on-screen virtual numeric keypad for Section B numerical questions.\n\n- **CBT Action Control Bar**:\n  - **Save & Next**: Commits the candidate\'s response, marks the status as **Answered** (Green), and advances to the next question.\n  - **Mark for Review & Next**: Marks the question as **Answered & Marked** (Purple with green checkmark) if an option is selected, or **Marked for Review** (Purple circle) if unselected, advancing forward.\n  - **Clear Response**: Clears selected options and resets the status back to **Not Answered** (Red).\n  - **Back / Next & Submit**: Standard NTA navigation controls.\n\n- **Question Palette (75 Questions) & 5 Official NTA States**:\n  - Designed the right sidebar housing all 75 question buttons with official shapes and colors:\n    1. **Not Visited**: Neutral white/slate with border\n    2. **Not Answered**: Official NTA Red\n    3. **Answered**: Official NTA Green\n    4. **Marked for Review**: Official NTA Purple circle\n    5. **Answered & Marked for Review**: Purple circle with an overlaid bright green checkmark badge *(considered for evaluation)*\n  - Live summary counter box reflecting instantaneous counts across all 5 states.\n  - Collapsible sidebar toggle to expand question viewport to full-width when needed.\n\n- **Per-Question Timing Telemetry in Local State**:\n  - Integrated active per-question timers tracking exact seconds and visit counts for each of the 75 questions in local state and persistent browser storage.\n  - Displayed a live timer on the active question viewport (`Time: MM:SS`).\n  - Added an **Exam Summary & Telemetry Analytics Modal** providing subject-wise breakdown tables, per-question duration logs, average time per question, and post-submission scoring with detailed solutions."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
