  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Submission Process**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user\'s request. Adding the \"Submit\" button and confirmation modal for the NTA JEE Main React app is the current priority. The simulation of the test submission and the subsequent display of a mock results page, or a success message is the intended outcome.\n\n\n**Implementing Submission Workflow**\n\nThe submission process is now taking shape, focusing on the confirmation modal. It will display key stats: Total Attempted, Marked for Review, and Unvisited. Upon confirmation, I\'ll freeze responses, stop the timer, and route to a results dashboard. Analytics and the SLP are next. I\'m prioritizing the UI flow and data capture for now.\n\n\n**Defining Results and Metrics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the data displayed post-submission. The dashboard will show total score, accuracy, attempted vs. unattempted breakdown, and percentile estimate. I am detailing the subject and chapter-wise breakdown of results. Each question is being tagged with a chapter to allow for more granular insights.\n\n\n**Detailing Actionable Insights**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into actionable insights for the user. I\'m focusing on providing chapter-wise details including accuracy, time spent, and question counts, as well as two new key metrics: \"Silly Mistakes\" (fast, incorrect answers) and \"Time Traps\" (questions where too much time was spent). I\'m planning to flag these, offer recommendations, and roll that into an automated SLP.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 421818596
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
