          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A circular coil of radius $R$ carries a steady current $I$. The magnetic field at its centre is $B_0$. The distance along its axis from the centre where the magnetic field reduces to $\\\\frac{B_0}{8}$ is:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$\\\\sqrt{3} R$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$2\\\\sqrt{2} R$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$3 R$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$\\\\frac{R}{\\\\sqrt{3}}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'$B(x) = \\\\frac{\\\\mu_0 I R^2}{2(R^2 + x^2)^{3/2}} = \\\\frac{B_0 R^3}{(R^2+x^2)^{3/2}}$. Setting $\\\\frac{B_0}{(1 + x^2/R^2)^{3/2}} = \\\\frac{B_0}{8} \\\\implies (1 + x^2/R^2)^{3/2} = 8 \\\\implies 1 + x^2/R^2 = 4 \\\\implies x = \\\\sqrt{3} R$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 8,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A block of mass $2\\\\text{ kg}$ is attached to a massless spring of force constant $k = 200\\\\text{ N/m}$. The block is pulled by a distance $x_0 = 0.1\\\\text{ m}$ on a frictionless horizontal plane and released at $t=0$. The maximum kinetic energy of the oscillator is:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$1.0\\\\text{ J}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$2.0\\\\text{ J}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$0.5\\\\text{ J}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$4.0\\\\text{ J}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'$E_{\\\\text{total}} = K_{\\\\max} = \\\\frac{1}{2} k x_0^2 = \\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\times 200 \\\\times (0.1)^2 = 1.0\\\\text{ J}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 9,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'An electric dipole with dipole moment $\\\\vec{p} = p_0 \\\\hat{i}$ is placed in an electric field $\\\\vec{E} = E_0 (\\\\hat{i} + \\\\sqrt{3}\\\\hat{j})$. The torque $\\\\vec{\\\\tau}$ acting on the dipole is:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$\\\\sqrt{3} p_0 E_0 \\\\hat{k}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$-\\\\sqrt{3} p_0 E_0 \\\\hat{k}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$p_0 E_0 \\\\hat{k}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$2 p_0 E_0 \\\\hat{j}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'Torque $\\\\vec{\\\\tau} = \\\\vec{p} \\\\times \\\\vec{E} = (p_0 \\\\hat{i}) \\\\times (E_0\\\\hat{i} + \\\\sqrt{3}E_0\\\\hat{j}) = \\\\sqrt{3} p_0 E_0 (\\\\hat{i} \\\\times \\\\hat{j}) = \\\\sqrt{3} p_0 E_0 \\\\hat{k}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 10,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A rod of length $L$ and uniform cross-sectional area $A$ has thermal conductivity $K$. If the temperature difference between its ends is maintained at $\\\\Delta T = 50^\\\\circ\\\\text{C}$, the rate of heat flow $\\\\frac{dQ}{dt}$ is directly proportional to:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$\\\\frac{A}{L}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$\\\\frac{L}{A}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$A \\\\cdot L$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$\\\\frac{1}{A L}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'By Fourier\\\'s Law of conduction, $\\\\frac{dQ}{dt} = \\\\frac{K A \\\\Delta T}{L}$, which is proportional to $\\\\frac{A}{L}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 11,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A satellite of mass $m$ revolves in a circular orbit around Earth of mass $M$ and radius $R$ at a height $h = R$ above the Earth\342\200\231s surface. The binding energy of the satellite is:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$\\\\frac{G M m}{4 R}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$\\\\frac{G M m}{2 R}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$\\\\frac{G M m}{8 R}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$\\\\frac{2 G M m}{R}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'Orbital radius $r = R + h = 2R$. Total energy $E = -\\\\frac{GMm}{2r} = -\\\\frac{GMm}{4R}$. Binding energy is $|E| = \\\\frac{GMm}{4R}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 12,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
