          text: "    type: \'NUMERICAL\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A solid sphere of mass $M = 5\\\\text{ kg}$ and radius $R = 0.2\\\\text{ m}$ rolls without slipping down an inclined plane of angle $\\\\theta = 30^\\\\circ$. The linear acceleration of the center of mass of the sphere is $a = \\\\frac{n}{7} g \\\\sin\\\\theta$. Find the integer value of $n$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'5\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'For pure rolling on incline, $a = \\\\frac{g \\\\sin\\\\theta}{1 + I_{\\\\text{cm}}/(MR^2)}$. For solid sphere, $I_{\\\\text{cm}} = \\\\frac{2}{5} MR^2$, so $a = \\\\frac{g \\\\sin\\\\theta}{1 + 2/5} = \\\\frac{5}{7} g \\\\sin\\\\theta$. Hence $n = 5$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: 0 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 22,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
