  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Dashboard Metrics**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the specific metrics needed for the Analytics & SLP Dashboard component. The critical path involves metrics calculated upon confirmation: timer end, response freeze, and routing to the dashboard. The dashboard\'s calculations are the next piece.\n\n\n**Calculating Score & Breakdown**\n\nI\'ve finalized the scoring logic, including the +4/-1 scheme, and the display of total score, attempted questions, and accuracy. I\'m now designing the chapter-wise breakdown. I\'m grouping questions by chapter and subject to calculate accuracy, correct, incorrect, and unattempted counts per chapter. I plan to present these results, along with the total questions for each subject, in the dashboard.\n\n\n**Analyzing Time Spent**\n\nI\'ve formulated two new metrics: a \"Silly Mistakes\" counter, identifying rushed incorrect answers, and a \"Time Traps\" counter, flagging questions where excessive time was spent. My focus is on the definitions for each of these two new metrics. For the silly mistakes counter, the threshold is less than 45 seconds spent and the question was incorrect. This is also known as: `isAttempted && !isCorrect && timeSpentSeconds < 45`. The time traps, as the name implies, will have a threshold of questions with more than 210 seconds spent.\n\n\n**Refining Time Trap Insights**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into \"Time Trap\" analysis. I\'m calculating the total time wasted on these traps and presenting a breakdown of correctly answered versus incorrectly or abandoned questions within that time frame. The next step is clearly flagging these time-consuming questions for future review and strategic adjustments.\n\n\n**Developing Dashboard Interactions**\n\nI\'m working on the interactive features for the Analytics Dashboard, thinking through the navigation tabs (\"Overview & SLP,\" \"Chapter Breakdown,\" \"Question-by-Question Solutions\") and filtering options within the solution view (All, Incorrect, Silly Mistakes, Time Traps, Correct). I\'m planning to use full KaTeX LaTeX rendering for comprehensive display of questions, responses, and solutions, and incorporating action buttons for test re-takes and report exports.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 27
      nanos: 875579252
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
