          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'For a negatively charged colloid, the flocculating ion is a cation. Higher valency gives greater coagulating power: $\\\\text{Al}^{3+} > \\\\text{Mg}^{2+} > \\\\text{Na}^+$.\',"
