          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A Carnot engine has an efficiency of $\\\\eta = 40\\\\%$ when its sink is at $T_c = 300\\\\text{ K}$. To increase the efficiency to $50\\\\%$, keeping sink temperature constant, the source temperature must be raised by:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$100\\\\text{ K}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$50\\\\text{ K}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$200\\\\text{ K}$\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$150\\\\text{ K}$\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'Initial: $1 - \\\\frac{300}{T_h} = 0.4 \\\\implies T_h = 500\\\\text{ K}$. Desired: $1 - \\\\frac{300}{T_h\\\'} = 0.5 \\\\implies T_h\\\' = 600\\\\text{ K}$. Rise $\\\\Delta T_h = 600 - 500 = 100\\\\text{ K}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 20,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    section: \'Section A\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \'MCQ\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    questionText: \'A plane electromagnetic wave propagating along the $+z$ direction has its electric field given by $\\\\vec{E} = E_0 \\\\cos(kz - \\\\omega t) \\\\hat{i}$. The corresponding magnetic field $\\\\vec{B}$ is oriented along:\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    options: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'1\', label: \'$+\\\\hat{j}$ direction\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'2\', label: \'$-\\\\hat{j}$ direction\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'3\', label: \'$+\\\\hat{k}$ direction\' },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      { id: \'4\', label: \'$-\\\\hat{i}$ direction\' }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    correctAnswer: \'1\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    explanation: \'Poynting vector $\\\\vec{S} \\\\propto \\\\vec{E} \\\\times \\\\vec{B}$ must point along propagation direction $\\\\hat{k}$. Since $\\\\vec{E}$ is along $\\\\hat{i}$, $\\\\hat{i} \\\\times \\\\hat{j} = \\\\hat{k}$, so $\\\\vec{B}$ is along $+\\\\hat{j}$.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    marks: { correct: 4, incorrect: -1 }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  // Section B: Physics Numerical (21 - 25)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: 21,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subject: \'Physics\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
