  planner_response {
    response: "I have enhanced the NTA JEE Main CBT application with the requested final submission workflow, confirmation modal, and comprehensive Analytics & Student Learning Plan (SLP) dashboard:\n\n- **Submit Button & Confirmation Modal**:\n  - Added a prominent **Submit** action in both the bottom footer control bar and the right sidebar palette.\n  - Clicking **Submit** opens a confirmation dialog asking: *\"Are you sure you want to submit?\"*\n  - The modal provides instant diagnostic stats required for final review:\n    - **Total Attempted**: Count of questions marked as *Answered* and *Answered & Marked for Review* out of 75.\n    - **Marked for Review**: Combined count of *Marked for Review* and *Answered & Marked for Review*.\n    - **Unvisited**: Count of untouched questions.\n    - **Not Answered / Visited but Skipped**: Count of questions seen without a recorded response.\n    - Subject-wise attempted counts (Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics).\n\n- **Submission Execution & Response Freeze**:\n  - When confirmed, the countdown timer terminates and is locked.\n  - All candidate responses across the 75 questions are permanently frozen into read-only mode, preventing accidental alterations post-test.\n  - The app routes to the **Analytics & SLP Dashboard** view (with an option to inspect the frozen CBT Question Palette and solutions).\n\n- **Analytics & SLP Dashboard Engine**:\n  - **Total Score**: Calculates score under the official `+4 / -1` marking scheme (+4 for correct, -1 for incorrect MCQ, 0 for unattempted) with accuracy percentage and percentile estimation.\n  - **Chapter-Wise Breakdown**: Detailed matrix across Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics (e.g. *Rotational Motion*, *AC Circuits*, *Thermodynamics*, *Coordination Compounds*, *Chemical Kinetics*, *Definite Integrals*, *Matrices & Determinants*), tracking questions, attempted, accuracy %, net score, and time spent.\n  - **\"Silly Mistakes\" Counter**: Explicitly flags questions where the candidate spent **less than 45 seconds** and received negative marks (`<45s wrong`), calculating estimated marks lost to rushed calculation errors.\n  - **\"Time Traps\" Counter**: Identifies questions where the candidate remained stuck for **more than 3.5 minutes** (`>210s`), highlighting high-friction problems that drained valuable exam time.\n\n- **3-Point Automated Student Learning Plan (SLP)**:\n  - **Recommendation 1: Priority Conceptual Revision**: Synthesizes the 2\342\200\2233 chapters with the lowest accuracy / highest negative scores and generates tailored 7-day revision directives and recommended problem sets.\n  - **Recommendation 2: Time Trap Mitigation**: Actionable pacing framework advising on the 2-minute triage rule and deferring heavy Section B numerical questions to second-pass solving.\n  - **Recommendation 3: Silly Mistake Eradication**: Enforces a 15-second verification protocol (checking SI units, negative prompt keywords like \"INCORRECT\", and calculation steps) to recover lost marks.\n  - **Question-by-Question Solution Inspector**: Full KaTeX LaTeX rendering of all 75 questions, candidate choices, official keys, and step-by-step solutions with filters for *Silly Mistakes*, *Time Traps*, and *Incorrect* responses."
    modified_response: "I have enhanced the NTA JEE Main CBT application with the requested final submission workflow, confirmation modal, and comprehensive Analytics & Student Learning Plan (SLP) dashboard:\n\n- **Submit Button & Confirmation Modal**:\n  - Added a prominent **Submit** action in both the bottom footer control bar and the right sidebar palette.\n  - Clicking **Submit** opens a confirmation dialog asking: *\"Are you sure you want to submit?\"*\n  - The modal provides instant diagnostic stats required for final review:\n    - **Total Attempted**: Count of questions marked as *Answered* and *Answered & Marked for Review* out of 75.\n    - **Marked for Review**: Combined count of *Marked for Review* and *Answered & Marked for Review*.\n    - **Unvisited**: Count of untouched questions.\n    - **Not Answered / Visited but Skipped**: Count of questions seen without a recorded response.\n    - Subject-wise attempted counts (Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics).\n\n- **Submission Execution & Response Freeze**:\n  - When confirmed, the countdown timer terminates and is locked.\n  - All candidate responses across the 75 questions are permanently frozen into read-only mode, preventing accidental alterations post-test.\n  - The app routes to the **Analytics & SLP Dashboard** view (with an option to inspect the frozen CBT Question Palette and solutions).\n\n- **Analytics & SLP Dashboard Engine**:\n  - **Total Score**: Calculates score under the official `+4 / -1` marking scheme (+4 for correct, -1 for incorrect MCQ, 0 for unattempted) with accuracy percentage and percentile estimation.\n  - **Chapter-Wise Breakdown**: Detailed matrix across Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics (e.g. *Rotational Motion*, *AC Circuits*, *Thermodynamics*, *Coordination Compounds*, *Chemical Kinetics*, *Definite Integrals*, *Matrices & Determinants*), tracking questions, attempted, accuracy %, net score, and time spent.\n  - **\"Silly Mistakes\" Counter**: Explicitly flags questions where the candidate spent **less than 45 seconds** and received negative marks (`<45s wrong`), calculating estimated marks lost to rushed calculation errors.\n  - **\"Time Traps\" Counter**: Identifies questions where the candidate remained stuck for **more than 3.5 minutes** (`>210s`), highlighting high-friction problems that drained valuable exam time.\n\n- **3-Point Automated Student Learning Plan (SLP)**:\n  - **Recommendation 1: Priority Conceptual Revision**: Synthesizes the 2\342\200\2233 chapters with the lowest accuracy / highest negative scores and generates tailored 7-day revision directives and recommended problem sets.\n  - **Recommendation 2: Time Trap Mitigation**: Actionable pacing framework advising on the 2-minute triage rule and deferring heavy Section B numerical questions to second-pass solving.\n  - **Recommendation 3: Silly Mistake Eradication**: Enforces a 15-second verification protocol (checking SI units, negative prompt keywords like \"INCORRECT\", and calculation steps) to recover lost marks.\n  - **Question-by-Question Solution Inspector**: Full KaTeX LaTeX rendering of all 75 questions, candidate choices, official keys, and step-by-step solutions with filters for *Silly Mistakes*, *Time Traps*, and *Incorrect* responses."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
